From a6e63f7a18cc2708d5731ce3ed7acb0cc8a1b4f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:11:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] qualcommax: ipq60xx: add support for Arista W-318

Arista W-318 is a Wi-Fi 6E wall-plate access point with a 2.5 GbE PoE
uplink and three 1 GbE LAN ports.

Hardware specification:
- SoC: Qualcomm IPQ6010 (4x Cortex-A53), on the IPQ6018 AP-CP01-C3
  reference design
- RAM: 2 GiB DDR4
- Flash: 32 MiB SPI NOR (Macronix MX25U25635F), 4 GiB eMMC (GPT)
- Ethernet:
  - uplink: 2.5 GbE (QCA8081), PoE in (802.3bt)
  - lan1-lan3: 1 GbE (QCA8075); lan1 can supply PoE
- Wi-Fi:
  - IPQ6010: 2.4 GHz 2x2 and 5 GHz 2x2 802.11ax
  - QCN9072 (PCIe): 6 GHz 2x2 802.11ax (the QCN9074's 2x2 sibling,
    same 17cb:1104)
- Bluetooth LE: Nordic nRF52833 (HCI over UART)
- TPM: TPM 2.0 (SPI)
- USB: 1x USB 3.0 Type-A
- LEDs: power (green, amber), uplink (green, orange), 2.4 GHz, 5 GHz,
  6 GHz (green), one for the three LAN ports (green, amber)
- Button: reset
- UART: RJ-45 console port, RS-232 levels, 115200 8N1

MAC addresses:
- uplink: 0:ART 0x0 (label)
- lan1: 0:ART 0x12 (label - 3); lan2: 0x0c (label - 2); lan3: 0x06
  (label - 1)
- Wi-Fi: from the calibration data

Calibration data for both Wi-Fi chips is read from 0:ART through NVMEM
cells (0x1000 and 0x26800).

The panel numbers the LAN ports the other way round from the PHYs:
lan1 is switch port 4 (PHY 3), lan3 switch port 2 (PHY 1). The uplink
alone is in the LAN by default, so that a LAN port cabled back to the
uplink's switch makes no loop; add the LAN ports to br-lan as needed.

Flash layout: the stock firmware keeps two slots: slot 0 with its
kernel in SPI NOR 0:HLOS and its root in the eMMC partition "rootfs",
slot 1 in 0:HLOS_1 and "rootfs_1", each with a data partition
("rootfs_data", "rootfs_data_1"). OpenWrt takes slot 0 (its overlay is
an f2fs on "rootfs_data"); slot 1 stays as a fallback.

Flash instructions (console needed):
1. Stop U-Boot: it waits 2 s and stops only for the string
   s6.D5r4Gnb89ZEWSW6Kq.
   Do not let the stock firmware boot meanwhile: its boot script saves
   the U-Boot environment on every boot.
2. Boot the initramfs from a TFTP server (nothing is saved):
     setenv ipaddr <AP address>; setenv serverip <TFTP server>
     setenv bootargs console=ttyMSM0,115200n8 rootwait panic=0
     tftpboot 0x60000000 openwrt-qualcommax-ipq60xx-arista_w-318-initramfs-uImage.itb
     bootm 0x60000000#config@cp01-c3
3. Back up all MTD partitions and the eMMC; 0:ART holds the unit's
   calibration data and MAC addresses and exists nowhere else.
4. Set the boot command, in one environment write:
     fw_setenv -s - <<'EOF'
     owrt_args console=ttyMSM0,115200n8 root=/dev/mmcblk0p1 rootwait panic=10
     owrt_load sf probe && sf read 0x60000000 0x7a0000 0x800000
     owrt_boot run owrt_load && setenv bootargs ${owrt_args} && bootm 0x60000000#config@cp01-c3
     arista_args setenv bootargs console=ttyMSM0,115200n8 root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 rootwait rw
     arista_boot run arista_args; setenv pri 1; setenv sr 0; run ubootscriptv2
     bootcmd run owrt_boot; run arista_boot
     pri 1
     EOF
5. Copy the sysupgrade image to /tmp, write it and reboot:
     sysupgrade -n /tmp/openwrt-qualcommax-ipq60xx-arista_w-318-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
   It writes the kernel to 0:HLOS and the root to "rootfs", and clears
   the start of "rootfs_data".

The stock boot (bootipq) checks image signatures; this boot command
loads OpenWrt's kernel from 0:HLOS with bootm instead and falls back to
the stock boot with pri=1, slot 1. The stock boot script saves the
environment, so the fallback first puts the stock bootargs back, and
clears its retry counter so that it never switches to slot 0. Later
upgrades are ordinary sysupgrades: the kernel goes to 0:HLOS (by its
/dev/mtdN path, since mtd reads "0:HLOS" as two devices), the root to
"rootfs", the settings to "rootfs_data".

Return to stock: fw_setenv bootcmd 'run ubootscriptv2', then reboot;
the stock firmware in slot 1 boots.

Known limitations:
- The QCN9072 starts only with Arista's own build of its firmware,
  which a following commit copies from the stock firmware in slot 1.
- lan1's PoE output (enabled by GPIO 48 low) stays off.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
